DocStudioRedactHelp = Redact: draw the zones to hide. When saving, the pages concerned become images (their text can no longer be selected), then DocStudio checks that the hidden text is no longer in the file. A black rectangle drawn with the Draw tool is not a redaction: it can be removed in any PDF reader.
DocStudioRedactImpact = Redaction: every page with a redacted zone is replaced by an image of the page. On these pages, the text can no longer be selected, copied nor found by a search, links and form fields disappear, the file gets heavier and small text may print less sharply. The new file keeps neither the metadata, the bookmarks, the attachments of the PDF nor its previous versions. If you replace the original, the copies already sent or filed elsewhere do not change. An electronic signature of the PDF is lost.
DocStudioCropHelp = Crop: draw the zone to keep. What lies outside the frame is only hidden, it stays in the file: to remove information, use redaction.
DocStudioCropImpact = Crop: what lies outside the frame is only hidden, it stays in the file.
